    "findings": [
      {
        "id": "acceptable-conditional",
        "title": "Acceptable and conditional upper values",
        "detail": "The higher permissible column is conditional on absence of an alternative source. Colour and sulphate add further conditions. It is not a routine substitute for the acceptable reference."
      },
      {
        "id": "iron-manganese",
        "title": "Iron–manganese interpretation remains open",
        "detail": "Amendment 1 changes the iron cell from 0.3 to 1.0 mg/L. The original Fe + Mn combined 0.3 mg/L remarks remain in the retrieved text; none of amendments 1–4 removes them. Both are retained for clarification."
      },
      {
        "id": "chlorine-direction",
        "title": "Residual chlorine is a minimum",
        "detail": "The chlorinated-water row specifies a consumer-end minimum and a separate viral-protection minimum. Its second-column value is preserved as printed; the helper does not turn it into a general maximum."
      },
      {
        "id": "uranium-scope",
        "title": "Uranium is separate from alpha/beta activity",
        "detail": "Amendment 3 adds uranium to Table 3 at 0.03 mg/L without relaxation. Amendment 4 changes its method options. It is not automatically removed by the ingredient-water FAQ radioactive-parameter wording; that applicability question requires confirmation."
      },
      {
        "id": "methods-and-guidance",
        "title": "Methods and sample volumes matter",
        "detail": "Amendments 2–3 update bacteriology to IS 15185 and distinguish operative MS2 requirements from guidance clauses. The eight microbial/biological entries retain 100 mL, 1 L and 10 L sample bases and their water-system scopes."
      },
      {
        "id": "date-discrepancy",
        "title": "Document dates take precedence in this reference",
        "detail": "The BIS page lists amendment 3 under 2020, but the downloaded amendment heading reads February 2021. Amendment 4 is headed November 2021. The earlier metadata inventory is retained as history, not used as the amendment text date."
      }
    ],
